  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing the probability of the maximum outcome: Lottery A has a 33% chance of 2500 Euros (maximum), Lottery B has a 100% chance of 2400 Euros (maximum). The reason prefers the lottery with the lower probability of the maximum outcome — i.e., A. However, the individual's report does not mention the probability of the maximum outcome at all. Instead, the individual focuses on the risk and the certainty of the outcome, indicating a preference for safety (Lottery B). This suggests the individual used a different reason — risk aversion or preference for certainty — rather than the one based on the probability of the maximum outcome. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process.",
